# Python API

Layout under `src/cctv/`: `api` (HTTP), `tools` (schemas + executors), `fetch` (stills), `analysis` (`chat_with_tools`), `config` (YAML catalog + overlay).

## Tools

Default model tools are `list_cameras`, `get_camera_image`, and `submit_answer`. Optional tools follow config flags (`internet` → `web_search`, `weather` → `get_weather`, `maps` → `search_map` / `reverse_geocode`). `submit_answer` is the only successful end of a chat turn.

`get_image` is the fetch helper used by `get_camera_image` and camera metadata analysis. Do not register it or add it to `_BASE_NAMES`:

```python
# BAD — model would call low-level fetch
_BASE_NAMES = ("list_cameras", "get_camera_image", "submit_answer", "get_image")

# GOOD
_BASE_NAMES = ("list_cameras", "get_camera_image", "submit_answer")
```

New tools: schema + executor in `src/cctv/tools/`, register in `__init__.py`, add tests under `tests/`.

## Frames and config

- Persist JPEGs on disk; serve via path-safe `GET /api/images/...`. Do not put large base64 blobs in JSON transcripts.
- `GET/PUT /api/config` merges `configs/cameras.yaml` and `configs/agent.yaml` with their gitignored `*.local.yaml` overlays. Never commit an overlay.

Runtime details: [`docs/AGENT.md`](docs/AGENT.md).
